    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-2941",
      "problem": "The area of the rectangular field shown below is $2\\,400\\,\\textrm{m}^2.$ What is the value of $x?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14195146/assets/9419ae4a3099216109bff99906e5d1724a8f01f61e48e22edc62c0e1b62a1bef.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The area of a rectangle is given by \n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = a \\cdot b,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are the lengths of the sides.\n\nFrom the figure, we obtain that \n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = 2\\,400\\mathrm{m}^2, \\qquad a = 60\\,\\mathrm{m}, \\qquad b=x .\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =a\\cdot b \\\\ 2\\,400 & =60\\cdot x \\\\ x & =\\frac{2\\,400}{60} \\\\ x & =40\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
